13-3-9:
Right sideThe sea (v. 2) was set in the court at the southeast corner of the
Temple. In Hebrew, directions are given from the standpoint of an individual facing east;
thus the right side indicates the south. Compare 1 Kings 7:39. See on Gen. 23:19; Ex. 3:1.

13-14-3:
Did turnWhen in their straits the people turned to God, He heard their prayers and
was gracious to them, delivering them from the hands of their enemies (see Ps. 106:44;
107:6).

13-31-27:
Corn, and wine, and oilThese are repeatedly mentioned together as the
outstanding fruitage of the land and the tokens of the blessings of Heaven (2 Chron. 31:5;
Num. 18:12; Deut. 7:13; Neh. 5:11; Jer. 31:12; etc.; cf. Rev. 6:6).

13-31-28:
For God had givenGod gives men power to get wealth and opens His bountiful
hand that they may share of His treasures (see Gen. 24:35; 1 Chron. 29:12; Job 42:12;
Prov. 10:22).

13-34-16:
Kept the passoverThe Passover was kept on the 14th of Nisan, and the Feast of
Unleavened Bread was observed from the 15th to the 21st days of the month (Ex. 12:18;
Lev. 23:5–8; Num. 28:16, 17).
